=Accessible Justice by Design=

Accessibility should be built into judicial services rather than
added after deployment.

== Dimensions ==

* physical;
* digital;
* linguistic;
* cognitive;
* informational;
* assisted access.

== Principle ==

'''Digital by default does not mean digital only.'''

[[Category:Access to Justice]]

{{Knowledge|id=INIT-AI-AUDIT-FRAMEWORK|type=Governance Framework|domain=AI Governance|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=5|status=PROPOSED}}

= AI Audit Framework =
The AI Audit Framework is proposed to provide systematic assessment of judicial AI systems.

== Audit Dimensions ==

* purpose;
* data;
* model/service;
* performance;
* risk;
* security;
* human oversight;
* explainability;
* traceability;
* incident management.

== Lifecycle ==
'''Pre-deployment → Operational Audit → Periodic Review'''

{{Knowledge|id=INIT-AI-CASE-SUMMARISATION|type=Strategic Initiative|domain=Intelligent Court|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=5|status=PROPOSED}}

= AI Case Summarisation =
AI Case Summarisation is proposed to generate structured summaries of long judicial records for authorised users.

== Requirements ==

* source links;
* human validation;
* controlled deployment;
* defined risk tier;
* measurable outcome.

== Dependencies ==

* data quality;
* legal authority;
* cybersecurity;
* user training;
* interoperability.

== Governance ==
The system should have an explicit retirement criterion so that obsolete technology does not become a permanent institutional liability.

{{Knowledge|id=INIT-AI-CASE-TRIAGE|type=Strategic Initiative|domain=Intelligent Case Management|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=5|status=PROPOSED}}

= AI Case Triage =
AI Case Triage is proposed to support administrative identification and routing of cases.

== Intended Uses ==

* administrative categorisation;
* workload analysis;
* identification of processing requirements.

== Boundary ==
Triage must not determine judicial outcome or substitute for judicial authority.

== Controls ==

* human oversight;
* risk classification;
* auditability;
* performance monitoring;
* exception handling.

{{Knowledge
|id=AI-CHANGE-MANAGEMENT
|type=Lifecycle Governance
|domain=Judicial AI
|jurisdiction=Indonesia
|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045
|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft
|ai_readiness=5
|status=PROPOSED
}}

=AI Change Management=

AI systems should be reassessed when material changes occur.

== Change Triggers ==

* model change;
* prompt change;
* retrieval-source change;
* data change;
* vendor change;
* workflow change;
* major system update.

== Required Response ==

'''Change → Reassess → Test → Approve → Monitor'''

== Principle ==

An AI system is not a static asset.

[[Category:AI Lifecycle]]
[[Category:AI Governance]]

