=AI Competency Framework=

The framework defines role-specific competencies required for
responsible judicial AI use.

== Competency Domains ==

* AI literacy;
* prompt literacy;
* data literacy;
* legal-tech literacy;
* verification;
* ethics;
* cybersecurity;
* governance.

[[Category:AI Competency]]

{{Knowledge
|id=AI-DEPLOYMENT-GATE
|type=Deployment Governance
|domain=Judicial AI
|jurisdiction=Indonesia
|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045
|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft
|ai_readiness=5
|status=PROPOSED
}}

=AI Deployment Gate=

High-impact judicial AI should pass formal governance gates before
deployment.

== Gate Conditions ==

* defined problem;
* legal authority;
* risk assessment;
* impact assessment;
* security testing;
* data assessment;
* model evaluation;
* human oversight;
* user competency;
* incident procedure;
* audit plan;
* fallback;
* retirement criterion.

== Decision ==

'''Approve / Approve with Conditions / Pilot Only / Reject'''

[[Category:AI Governance]]
[[Category:Deployment]]

{{Knowledge|id=INIT-AI-DOCUMENT-CLASSIFICATION|type=Strategic Initiative|domain=Intelligent Court|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=5|status=PROPOSED}}

= AI Document Classification =
AI Document Classification is proposed to classify documents and support administrative routing.

== Control Mechanisms ==

* confidence thresholds;
* human exception handling;
* controlled pilot;
* quality evaluation;
* auditability.

== Boundary ==
The initiative is administrative.

It should not be interpreted as delegating judicial authority to an algorithm.

{{Knowledge|id=JUDICIAL-AI-GOVERNANCE|type=Governance Architecture|domain=AI Governance|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=5|status=PROPOSED}}

= Judicial AI Governance Architecture =
AI adoption in the judiciary requires governance before large-scale deployment.

== Governance Components ==

* AI inventory;
* risk classification;
* legal assessment;
* fundamental-rights assessment;
* data governance;
* procurement controls;
* vendor-risk management;
* cybersecurity;
* auditability;
* human oversight;
* incident reporting;
* independent evaluation.

== Decision Rule ==
Every significant AI deployment should have a clear:

'''Pilot → Evaluate → Scale or Stop'''

gate.

{{Knowledge|id=INIT-AI-LEGAL-RESEARCH|type=Strategic Initiative|domain=Intelligent Court|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=5|status=PROPOSED}}

= AI Legal Research Assistant =
The AI Legal Research Assistant is proposed as a source-grounded research-support capability.

== Core Functions ==

* retrieve approved legal sources;
* assist legal research;
* provide citation traceability;
* identify relevant legal materials;
* explicitly communicate uncertainty.

== Safeguard ==
The system supports research but does not replace legal judgement.

== Implementation Requirements ==

* defined problem;
* accountable owner;
* baseline;
* risk tier;
* measurable outcome;
* controlled pilot;
* data-quality assessment;
* legal-authority assessment;
* cybersecurity;
* user training;
* interoperability;
* retirement criterion.

{{Knowledge
