=AI Red-Team Testing=

Red-team testing deliberately attempts to identify weaknesses before
high-impact AI systems are deployed.

== Test Areas ==

* fabricated citations;
* unsafe outputs;
* prompt manipulation;
* data leakage;
* security weaknesses;
* inappropriate recommendations;
* bias;
* failure under unusual inputs.

== Output ==

Each identified weakness should be documented, assessed and assigned
a remediation owner.

[[Category:AI Security]]
[[Category:AI Assurance]]

{{Knowledge|id=INIT-AI-TIMELINE-EVIDENCE|type=Strategic Initiative|domain=Intelligent Court|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=5|status=PROPOSED}}

= AI Timeline and Evidence Mapping =
The initiative assists authorised users in organising dates, events and documents.

== Critical Boundary ==
The system must '''not determine evidentiary weight'''.

Its role is organisational and analytical assistance.

== Requirements ==

* source traceability;
* human validation;
* controlled pilot;
* defined risk tier;
* measurable outcome;
* cybersecurity;
* interoperability.

{{Knowledge|id=INIT-AI-TRANSLATION|type=Strategic Initiative|domain=Accessible Justice|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=5|status=PROPOSED}}

= AI Translation and Accessibility =
The initiative proposes controlled translation, transcription and accessibility support.

== Human Review ==
High-stakes outputs require human review.

== Potential Functions ==

* translation;
* transcription;
* accessibility support;
* multilingual information access.

== Governance Requirements ==

* defined purpose;
* risk classification;
* validation;
* human oversight;
* security;
* quality monitoring.

