=Algorithmic Impact Assessment=

Every high-impact judicial AI system should undergo an impact
assessment before deployment and periodically thereafter.

== Assessment ==

* purpose;
* affected persons;
* legal basis;
* data sources;
* model limitations;
* error modes;
* potential harms;
* discrimination risks;
* cybersecurity risks;
* human oversight;
* fallback procedures;
* monitoring indicators.

== Review Trigger ==

The assessment should be revisited after significant changes to models,
data, prompts, retrieval sources or vendors.

== Output ==

The assessment must produce an evidence record suitable for governance
and audit review.

[[Category:Impact Assessment]]
[[Category:AI Governance]]

