=Bias and Fairness Assessment=

High-impact judicial AI should be assessed for potential discriminatory
effects and unequal performance.

== Assessment ==

* affected groups;
* training/retrieval data;
* error distribution;
* differential performance;
* proxy variables;
* potential discriminatory effects;
* mitigation;
* monitoring.

== Principle ==

Fairness assessment must be contextualized to the actual judicial
use case.

[[Category:AI Fairness]]
[[Category:AI Ethics]]

{{Knowledge|id=BLUEPRINT-2010-2035-GAP-ANALYSIS|type=Gap Analysis|domain=Judicial Reform|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=4|status=PROPOSED}}

= Blueprint 2010–2035 Gap Analysis =
The transition to a future judiciary should identify the remaining gaps between the existing reform architecture and the proposed 2035–2045 target state.

== Gap Categories ==

* governance;
* process;
* technology;
* data;
* knowledge;
* workforce;
* AI;
* cybersecurity;
* access to justice;
* public trust.

== Output ==
'''Current State → Gap → Required Capability → Initiative → KPI'''

{{Knowledge|id=RENSTRA-ISS-3.2|type=Strategic Performance Indicator|domain=Public Financial Management|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Renstra Mahkamah Agung 2025–2029|evidence=E3 — Official Primary Source|ai_readiness=5|status=VERIFIED}}

= Budget Performance Value =
Indicator 3.2 measures budget performance.

== Composition ==
The value consists of:

* 50% Budget Planning Performance Value;
* 50% Budget Implementation Performance Value.

== Budget Planning ==
Includes:

* effectiveness;
* achievement of strategic performance indicators;
* effectiveness of Echelon I units;
* effectiveness of work units;
* efficiency.

== Budget Implementation ==
Includes:

* DIPA revisions;
* budget absorption;
* settlement of bills;
* SPM dispensations;
* DIPA page deviation;
* contractual expenditure;
* UP and TUP management;
* output achievement.

The indicator measures performance for the preceding year (t−1).

== Target ==
'''90''' for each year, 2025–2029.

