{{Knowledge|id=INIT-CASE-DURATION-ANALYTICS|type=Strategic Initiative|domain=Judicial Performance|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=5|status=PROPOSED}}

= Case Duration Analytics =
Case Duration Analytics is proposed to identify patterns in case processing time.

== Uses ==

* identify bottlenecks;
* compare workload patterns;
* support administrative improvement;
* identify areas requiring further investigation.

== Principle ==
Analytics should improve institutional performance without turning performance indicators into automated judicial decision rules.

{{Knowledge|id=BP-0005|type=Reform Framework|domain=Case Management|source=Cetak Biru Pembaruan Peradilan 2010-2035|source_page=35-44|evidence=E3 — Official Primary Source|ai_readiness=5|status=VERIFIED}}

= Case Management Reform Blueprint =
The Blueprint identifies case management as a major area of judicial technical and administrative reform.

== Strategic Objectives ==

* control case flows;
* improve efficiency;
* improve case administration;
* improve case information;
* support consistency and quality;
* improve judicial processes.

== Transformation Logic ==
'''Case Workload'''

↓

'''Process Reform'''

↓

'''Case Management'''

↓

'''Performance Improvement'''

{{Knowledge|id=RENSTRA-INDICATOR-1.1-DICTIONARY|type=Indicator Definition|domain=Case Management|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Renstra Mahkamah Agung 2025–2029|evidence=E3 — Official Primary Source|ai_readiness=5|status=VERIFIED}}

= Percentage of Timely Case Resolution =
The indicator measures timely case resolution according to applicable standards.

== Coverage ==
The dictionary specifies measurement for:

* cassation;
* judicial review;
* consideration of clemency;
* judicial review of regulations;
* jurisdictional disputes;
* opinion-review proceedings;
* electoral administrative violations;
* appellate proceedings;
* first-instance proceedings.

== Exclusions ==
Cases whose summons process is specifically governed by law, including certain mass-media summons and parties located overseas, are excluded from the calculation.

== Formula ==
<nowiki><math> \frac{\text{Cases resolved on time}} {\text{Cases resolved}}\times100\% </math></nowiki>

{{Knowledge|id=INIT-CASELAW-SEMANTIC-SEARCH|type=Strategic Initiative|domain=Judicial Knowledge Infrastructure|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=5|status=PROPOSED}}

= Case-Law Semantic Search =
Case-Law Semantic Search is proposed to enable retrieval based on meaning and legal concepts rather than keywords alone.

== Dependencies ==

* [[Judicial Knowledge Graph]];
* [[Indonesian Legal Ontology]];
* structured metadata;
* source validation;
* high-quality case-law data.

== Objective ==
Improve discovery of relevant judicial knowledge while preserving source traceability.

