[[Category:Knowledge Graph]]

{{Knowledge|id=CITATION-INTEGRITY|type=Quality Standard|domain=Judicial Knowledge|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=5|status=PROPOSED}}

= Citation Integrity =
Citation Integrity ensures that Wiki claims can be traced to the sources from which they were derived.

== Requirements ==

* precise source identification;
* stable reference;
* quotation accuracy;
* context preservation;
* version awareness;
* distinction between source and interpretation.

== AI Requirement ==
AI systems should provide source links or citations rather than presenting unsupported legal propositions.

{{Knowledge|id=CLAIM-REGISTRY|type=Evidence Registry|domain=Knowledge Governance|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Judicial Knowledge Wiki Architecture|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=5|status=PROPOSED}}

= Claim Registry =
The Claim Registry records substantive claims appearing in Wiki knowledge objects.

== Claim Fields ==

* claim ID;
* claim text;
* source;
* evidence level;
* date;
* jurisdiction;
* reviewer;
* verification status;
* related entities.

== Purpose ==
A claim should be traceable to the evidence supporting it.

== AI Use ==
AI-generated claims must remain distinguishable from verified institutional knowledge.

{{Knowledge|id=INIT-COI-INTELLIGENCE|type=Strategic Initiative|domain=Judicial Integrity|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=5|status=PROPOSED}}

= Conflict-of-Interest Intelligence =
