{{Knowledge|id=HUMAN-CENTRED-JUDICIARY|type=Transformation|domain=Human-Centred Justice|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=5|status=PROPOSED}}

= Human-Centred Judiciary =
The future judiciary should be designed around the needs of people rather than around the capabilities of technology.

== Principles ==

* citizen needs are the starting point;
* accessibility is designed into services;
* technology reduces unnecessary administrative burden;
* digital services remain understandable;
* human assistance remains available;
* efficiency must not undermine fundamental rights.

== Transformation ==
'''Technology for citizens'''

rather than

'''citizens adapting to technology'''.

{{Knowledge|id=INIT-HUMAN-IN-THE-LOOP|type=AI Governance Standard|domain=Judicial AI|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=5|status=PROPOSED}}

= Human-in-the-Loop Standard =
The Human-in-the-Loop Standard establishes human responsibility in AI-supported judicial workflows.

== Core Principle ==
'''AI output is assistance, not judicial authority.'''

== Minimum Controls ==

* identifiable human owner;
* review of high-impact outputs;
* ability to reject AI output;
* escalation mechanism;
* audit trail;
* uncertainty disclosure;
* incident reporting.

== Judicial Rule ==
The final exercise of judicial authority remains with the authorised human decision-maker.

