=Judicial AI Governance Council=

The Judicial AI Governance Council is proposed as the institutional
body responsible for AI policy, risk, standards and oversight.

== Proposed Functions ==

* AI policy;
* risk classification;
* standards;
* impact-assessment oversight;
* procurement governance;
* audit oversight;
* incident governance;
* deployment gates;
* competency requirements;
* strategic review.

== Relationship ==

The Council operates within the authority of Supreme Court leadership
and coordinates with:

* BSDK/capability functions;
* technology/data functions;
* courts;
* judges and professional users;
* independent evaluation functions.

== Principle ==

AI governance should remain institutional governance, not merely
technical administration.

[[Category:AI Governance]]
[[Category:Institutional Architecture]]

