{{Knowledge|id=JK-0109|type=Concept|domain=Judicial Knowledge|evidence=E3|ai_readiness=5|status=FOUNDATIONAL}}

= Judicial Concept =
A Judicial Concept represents a recurring idea or analytical category used to understand judicial institutions, processes, or decisions.

Examples include:

* judicial independence;
* judicial accountability;
* access to justice;
* case management;
* judicial integrity;
* court administration;
* judicial education.

{{Knowledge|id=JUDICIAL-COPILOT|type=AI Service|domain=Judicial AI|jurisdiction=Indonesia|source=Indonesia Judiciary Future Blueprint 2035–2045|evidence=E2 — Strategic Research Draft|ai_readiness=5|status=PROPOSED}}

= Judicial Copilot =
A Judicial Copilot is proposed as a controlled institutional AI service rather than an unrestricted chatbot.

== Requirements ==

* retrieve from approved sources;
* provide citations;
* preserve appropriate audit logs;
* clearly identify uncertainty;
* prevent autonomous exercise of judicial authority.

== Core Rule ==
'''AI recommends → Human verifies → Judge decides'''

